[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "2605171300", :adr/title "Open-UNSPSC Generative Agent Fleet using OpenRouter and Local Fallback", :adr/status "superseded", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "# ADR 2605171300: Open-UNSPSC Generative Agent Fleet using OpenRouter and Local Fallback\n\n## Status\nAccepted\n\n## Context\nThe `etzhayyim-project-open-unispsc` project requires specialized procurement and validation logic for over 150,000 distinct commodities (e.g., CAD validation for robotics, safety compliance for chemicals). Hardcoding this logic was unscalable. We needed an architecture to dynamically generate and execute these 150k specific LangGraph agents while maintaining high quality, safety (sandboxing), and reasonable infrastructure cost.\n\n## Decision\n1. **Physical Code Generation (AOT)**: We opted to use LLMs to generate physical Python files (e.g., `c23153100.py`) containing the LangGraph logic, saving them into the local repository under `unispsc_agents/`. This approach was favored over runtime string evaluation from the database because it allows for static type checking, code review, and leverages standard Python module loading.\n2. **Dynamic Runner**: `dynamic_runner.py` uses `importlib.import_module` to load these agents at runtime during the `runItemWorkflow` pipeline, falling back gracefully if an agent has not yet been generated.\n3. **OpenRouter High-Speed Bulk Generation**: To overcome the timeout and quality degradation issues observed with the local `gemma4:latest` model via Ollama during the generation of the 18,345 `ucalypt` subset, we switched the batch generation script (`run_batch_spec_gen.py`) to use `google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite` via OpenRouter. This enabled a concurrency of 10, completing over 18,000 high-quality agent generation tasks in under two hours for less than $35.\n4. **Local / Murakumo Fallback**: The generation pipeline preserves the ability to fall back to the Murakumo Mac mini GPU fleet (`gemma4-e4b`) or local Ollama if external API keys (`OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`) are unavailable.\n\n## Consequences\n- **Positive**: We achieved 100% coverage of the 18,345 target commodity subset with highly specialized logic. The physical file architecture ensures stability and reviewability.\n- **Negative**: The repository size increased slightly due to the addition of ~18k small Python files, and Git operations (like `git status`) take longer locally. We will monitor repository performance and consider a mono-repo split or submodules if performance degrades further.\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605171300-open-unspsc-generative-agent-fleet.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "open-unispsc-generative-agent-fleet", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-17", :adr/date "2026-05-17", :adr/superseded_by ["2606172100-retire-unispsc-python-per-code-fleet"]}]
